    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_section_what_title">What AllergyTrack does</string>
    <string name="about_section_what_content">AllergyTrack helps you identify the triggers of your allergies. You record what you eat, where you go and what allergic reactions you experience — the app then looks for patterns and correlations between this data.</string>
    <string name="about_section_how_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="about_section_how_content">Every day you log food (photo or manual entry), allergic symptoms (eczema, rhinitis, itching…) and the app automatically loads air quality and pollen data based on your GPS location. After collecting data, the analysis reveals what most often triggers your allergies.</string>
    <string name="about_section_data_title">Your data</string>
    <string name="about_section_data_content">All data is stored only on your device and is never shared with third parties. The app collects no personal data.</string>
    <string name="about_section_sources_title">Data sources</string>
    <string name="about_section_sources_content">Air quality and pollen data: Open-Meteo (open-meteo.com)\nFood database: Open Food Facts (openfoodfacts.org)</string>
    <string name="about_disclaimer">This application is not a medical device and does not provide medical diagnosis or treatment. For medical advice, always consult a qualified healthcare professional.</string>

